# API design

- Every business route lives under `/api/v1/<plural-kebab-noun>` (`/api/v1/projects`, `/api/v1/projects/:id`). Health stays at `/health/live` and `/health/ready`, outside `/api`, unversioned and without auth or rate limit.
- No verbs in paths except auth actions (`/auth/login`, `/auth/refresh`). The caller's own data is `/me` or a filter derived from the principal; never make a client send its own user id to mean "me".
- Status codes: `GET` 200, `POST` create 201 with the created DTO, `PATCH`/`PUT` 200 with the updated DTO, `DELETE` 204 with no body, idempotent actions 204. The status is chosen in `api/http/error-mapper.ts`, not in the domain.
- JSON fields are camelCase. Timestamps are ISO-8601 strings with offset. Ids are UUIDs. Never return database rows, password hashes, token hashes or internal flags. Presenters are an allow-list.
- Success bodies are `{ data, meta }`. Lists put the page in `data` and `{ nextCursor, limit }` in `meta` (`limit` default 20, max 100). A single resource uses `meta: {}`.
- Partial updates are `PATCH` with every field optional and at least one required. Do not accept the id, owner, role or timestamps in a body.
- Errors are `application/json`: `{ error: { code, message, details, requestId } }`. Clients branch on `code`. `requestId` matches the `X-Request-Id` response header.
- Breaking changes (removed field, renamed code, changed type) need a new version folder (`api/http/v2`) over the same domain. Additive changes do not.
- Every route has a `registry.registerPath()` in `src/api/http/openapi/document.ts` using the same Zod schemas that validate it, with its success and error responses and `security` for protected routes. A route without a docs entry is unfinished.

Procedure: `express-resource` skill. Docs: `openapi-docs` skill.
